#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0562 expect=violation domain=VS
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when REPNUM is in the dataset and there are multiple records for a subject for a test within the timeframe identified by the timing variables on the record, and --REPNUM is missing or not unique per subject per test per timing variables.
#note "PLAN-grouping-key-identity (signed zero, a missed finding): VISITNUM is the only Timing variable. One SYSBP record at VISITNUM -0.0 and one at 0.0 -- one value (IEEE 754: -0.0 == 0.0; register D84 works on the real value; owner: '-0 and 0 are to be treated as one key everywhere'), so one timing group of two records with an empty VSREPNUM -> rows 1 and 2 fire. Row 3 (VISITNUM 1.5) is a group of one and never fires. Before the plan the raw index split the two zeros into two one-record blocks and nothing fired. Since PLAN-negative-zero-on-load (NZL O1) a loaded -0.0 is 0.0; the rule-test harness keeps this cell raw on purpose, so it stands in for a computed -0.0 (GKI Q4)."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015 VSSEQ=1
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#library domain-variables VS USUBJID:Identifier VSTESTCD:Topic VISITNUM:Timing VSREPNUM:Qualifier DOMAIN:Identifier
dataset VS label="Vital Signs"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VSSEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col VSTESTCD type=Char label="Vital Signs Test Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num label="Visit Number"
col VSREPNUM type=Char label="Repetition Number"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | VS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | SYSBP | -0.0 |
CDISCPILOT01 | VS | 01-701-1015 | 2 | SYSBP | 0.0 |
CDISCPILOT01 | VS | 01-701-1015 | 3 | SYSBP | 1.5 |
---
